+// Per-dimension caps alone still allow a width/height pair (e.g. a generic region
+// or a single symbol-dictionary glyph) up to `MAX_DIMENSION * MAX_DIMENSION` (~4.3
+// billion pixels), which is cheap to specify in a tiny file but takes real wall-clock
